---
import { AGENDA } from "../../lib/contact";
import StudioLayout from "../../layouts/StudioLayout.astro";
import CartesCas from "../../components/studio/CartesCas.astro";
---
<StudioLayout
  titre='Automate what really costs you'
  description='Kigumi identifies the processes that weigh most on your company, deploys the agents that take them over, and measures the real gain.'
  actif="">
<section class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Process automation &middot; Small &amp; mid-sized companies</span>
    <h1>Automate what<br>really costs you.<br><span class="accent">And prove it.</span></h1>
    <div class="rule"></div>
    <p class="lead">Most AI projects never get past the pilot. Kigumi identifies the processes that weigh most on your company, deploys the agents that take them over, and measures the real gain. For companies of 50 to 300 people.</p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn" href={AGENDA} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Book a 45-minute pre-diagnosis</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/en/method/">See the method</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="tint">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">What we take over</p>
    <h2>Three examples, among many others</h2>
    <p class="lead">Processes we have already studied in detail. The criterion isn&rsquo;t your industry, it&rsquo;s the shape of the work: repetitive, high-volume, and dependent on knowledge nobody has written down.</p>
    <div style="margin-top:34px"><CartesCas /></div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin-top:24px;font-size:14px">Illustrative examples, built from situations observed in these industries. No missions delivered to date.</p>
    <p style="margin-top:14px"><a href="/en/use-cases/">See every case, by process and by role &rarr;</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="tint">
  <div class="wrap">
   <div class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Who does the work</p>
    <h2>Thirty years in the trade, between two people</h2>
    <p>Julien ran customer relations at a software publisher — support, complex projects, a team of eleven. St&eacute;phane ran all of its development teams there, R&amp;D and machine learning included, on products used by millions of people.</p>
    <p>We spent three years there together, at the two ends of the same product: one took the calls when it didn&rsquo;t do what it was said to do, the other led the teams that had built it.</p>
    <p><strong>The two people who sell you the mission are the two who deliver it.</strong> No junior consultant assigned at kick-off, no subcontracting.</p>
    <p style="margin-top:1.4em"><a href="/en/about/">Who we are &rarr;</a></p>
   </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">How we work</p>
    <h2>Three principles, kept on every mission</h2>
    <div class="grid" style="margin-top:34px">
      <div><h3>A costed diagnosis, never a prototype</h3><p class="muted">We start by estimating what each process costs you, and we rank them. You can stop there and use the report without us.</p></div>
      <div><h3>We only build what the process requires</h3><p class="muted">Nothing generic, nothing built just in case. The knowledge base follows the real need, not the other way round.</p></div>
      <div><h3>We measure the real gain, and we show it to you</h3><p class="muted">Every quarter, a report compares what was gained with what was projected. Including when the gap isn&rsquo;t in our favour.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/en/method/">The method in detail</a></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cta">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>45 minutes to find out whether it&rsquo;s worth it</h2>
    <p>We look at your processes and tell you which one costs you the most. You leave with that ranking, whether we work together or not — and if nothing at your company is worth automating, we&rsquo;ll tell you.</p>
    <div class="btn-row"><a class="btn" href={AGENDA} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Book a call</a></div>
  </div>
</section>
</StudioLayout>
